## ✅ English (Professional Translation)

I created a Java project in which I added Hibernate-related dependencies.

### 🔹 Hibernate Configuration File

I created a Hibernate configuration file. This file is important because it helps us define:

* Where the database is located
* How Hibernate should connect to the database
* Hibernate settings and properties
* How data and schema updates should be handled

Hibernate automatically generates SQL queries and shows them in the output.

### 🔹 DDL (Data Definition Language)

DDL is a language that defines the structure of database tables, such as:

* Creating tables
* Defining columns
* Adding constraints

### 🔹 hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto = update

If any structural change happens in the entity/class, it should also be updated in the database.

That is why we use this property:

```xml
<property name="hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto">update</property>
```

### 🔹 show_sql & format_sql

* `show_sql` means Hibernate will print the generated SQL queries in the console
* `format_sql` means the SQL queries will be printed in a properly formatted and readable way

### 🔹 current_session_context_class = thread

```xml
<property name="hibernate.current_session_context_class">thread</property>
```

This means Hibernate automatically creates a session and binds it with the current application thread.

